A||||21||84fierotrevor||why does everyone hate ricers ?||||1||
Z||000000||84fierotrevor||11-08-2001||01:26 AM||||Why does every ne hate ricers?<BR>And why do ricers hate us ?<BR>It's like some kinda battle<BR>I mean don't get me wrong i love my fiero<BR>And my favoirte car in the world is the firebird.<BR>but my friend drives a 1998 eclipse<BR>and that thing is ****ing sweet and it looks nice too. Let alone it will kill any fiero stock to stock.<BR>is there somereson we all can't just sorta get along ?<BR>and how come every one hates ford too ?<BR>i must be missing somthing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||11-08-2001||01:34 AM||||Fieros are a GM product. <BR>Domestic vs Import and GM vs Ford has raged for years. <BR>It's not our fault, and on a "one-on-one" basis, some of us like Hondas, VWs, Mustangs, and even the occasional, transmission-exploding Eclipse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Hope that helps. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85-Sig-2.gif">              <BR><B><I><u><FONT COLOR="red">TRiAD Motorsports</FONT></u></B> \\\\ <B>triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> //// Michael ~ 85 GT 4sp</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||WhiteFieroBlur||11-08-2001||02:09 AM||||I posted a topic about this a lil while back called "Should we hate the rice?" <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003908.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003908.html</A>  I personally love a nice hooked up neons and civics. I mean its all I am around. I have never seen a nice lookin fiero before. I never understood why everyone hated the rice cars till I found out they hate the fake people with the fake rides. <P> I think my car is turning into a rice/fiero. I have that big white windshield vinyl and at the bottom is has the words of my car club and I was gonna put one of those big kit spoilers on there if it fitted.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||11-08-2001||02:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>Why does every ne hate ricers?<BR>And why do ricers hate us ?<BR>It's like some kinda battle<BR>I mean don't get me wrong i love my fiero<BR>And my favoirte car in the world is the firebird.<BR>but my friend drives a 1998 eclipse<BR>and that thing is ****ing sweet and it looks nice too. Let alone it will kill any fiero stock to stock.<BR>is there somereson we all can't just sorta get along ?<BR>and how come every one hates ford too ?<BR>i must be missing somthing.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not everyone HATES ricers, we may think SOME of them are misguided...<BR>SOME of them have very nice cars, and we can apreciate them!<BR>Some of them have rust buckets being held together with stickers, and we laugh at them!<BR>And you have everything inbetween...<P>Does anyone remember the AMC Pacer?<BR>I had one blow the doors off my Nova many years ago, and when I saw the supercharged engine sitting in the rear of the car, I could only think WTF!!??!!<BR>Not my cup of tea, but obviously the owner wanted it!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||11-08-2001||10:14 AM||||It all depends on what your definition of a "ricer" is.  For me, it boils down to one specific group and it does not matter whether they own imports or not, but they usually do.<P>They are the "enthusiasts" (I am giving them some credit here, maybe too much?) that love to pump money into visual mods, sometimes engine mods but more often then not only visual.  Then they take to the street with their stickered up, big winged, all-show no-go cars and act like their car is the greatest thing on the road and put down everybody elses car.  <P>Example:  They could own a Cavalier/Civic etc etc with a cheap Pep boys big 'ole exhaust tip with all kinds of stickers/decals, big tires and rims, maybe a wing, big deal on the back window and all with a stock 2.2L Four pounding out in the neighborhood of 120 noisy horses.  Then they will go out amd try to prove they have a great car by racing stock Saturns, Kia's, and probably their fair share of 5 year olds on tricicles so they have a few kill stories to talk about.  To cement the ricer label from me, they will then talk smack about any other possible car they can.  They label anything other than their stickered up econobox a POS, and then claimed to have beaten half the cars on the planet in races.<P>Even those with engine mods can be ricers too if they are flat out jerks about it and do it to put others down.  <P>I have all the respect in the world for any import owner who does any kind of modification to his car, and is basically not a jerk about it.<P>Its more of an attitude.  Not a specific car, or origin of nameplate.  (btw, there may well be ricers among us Fiero owners too!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||11-08-2001||10:25 AM||||The original and "official" definition of the term "rice" was/is;<BR><I>A vehicle that has been made to visually depict something that it is not.</I><BR>This can be a Civic with big "Edelbrock" sticker on it, with no Edelbrock parts to be found, a car of any kind (including the Mustangs I've seen) with something like "Type R" on it, when it in fact, is not, or any other intentionally "misleading" or incorrect labeling on a car. <P>That said, I like fformula's definition as well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Voytek||11-08-2001||10:34 AM||||While HATE may be a strong word, there is a lot of gray area here.  For example, some will call you a ricer if your shifter is chromed and you have neon around your license plate.  IS this a ricer?  Certainly not.<P>Like the other people have explained, it's all about attitute and 'all show no go'.<P>I, for one, find some 'riced-out' vehicles quite attractive (if done with taste) and the only thing I dislike is attitude.<P>Think about one more thing:  how would we try to make ourselved feel better if there weren't any rice-mobiles or Fords around?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||11-08-2001||11:10 AM||||Yeah, to me Rice is a poser.  Making your car "look" fast, rather than "be" fast.  Stickers and potato shooter exhausts on a completely stock car.  That's rice.  Modding your car for better performance, that's just good old hot rodding.  The times have changed, and so have the cars.  <P>One thing I've never understood.  Maybe someone who's done it can help me.  The vinyl windsheild banners.  I don't get it.  Ok, it's one thing is you're advertising something - your web site, car club, your dog's best friend's name - but so many of these cars have solid windshield banners on there with nothing on them.  I don't get it.  And I really don't get the ones with the banners at the bottom of the windshield.  This is seriously not a flame.  Can someone please enlighten me on how that could be cool?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000008||84fierotrevor||11-08-2001||12:56 PM||||So those guys i see at the street races<BR>that have all this wierd enggine ****  in there that makes it do funny noises and sound like a big semi truck coming to a stop, are not ricers ?<BR>those guys at the mall that have that huge ass wing on the back of there car and a big ass pipe that sounds like a bumble bee on steroieds, and a bunch of honda performance stickers,But no engine modifications is ?<BR>oooooohhh ! i see now.   I think im gonna be deemd a ricer cuss i wanna stick stickers on my 4 banger. lol i am gonna do a engine swap too, But i can offord the stickers quicker then i can the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tigger||11-08-2001||01:19 PM||||That's fine... just don't develop an attitude and you shouldn't have a problem.||||reg||7
Z||000010||Screwie||11-08-2001||02:39 PM||||I agree a ricer is all about attitude. Someone can make his car look good by putting on a nice spoiler, a nice looking exhaust and a chrome whatever. As long as he knows his car's performance doesn't change because of that and he doesn't put other peoples cars down, I don't think he'll qualify as a ricer. <P>Putting stickers like M3, VTEC on a Yugo is definitely making it something it's not. That's where I draw the line  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||11-08-2001||03:03 PM||||I don't "HATE" them. I just can't believe the things they do to a car. Example of idiot's by me. Early 90's Grand Prix. 12" wheels sticking out from the body. Blue Hyndai with Dodge "3.5 24-valve" decals on the side and a "V-8 Magnum" badge on the back. I think the "fart cans" are stupid.<BR>The latest crazy is the "combat wings" Some cars they look OK on, (Personally I don't like the design of the wings) But some people need a brain. What purpose does a wing that big on a late 80's Olds Calais with dents and rust? Especially when it has the base 4-cyl in at and the wing has more gloss than the windows on the car. I actually think someone here is offering some deal to put these wings on cars. Everyday more and more cars have them on. I first saw one on a yellow Mustang GT. When I first saw it I thought the wing was a little big but it wasn't bad and the yellow paint job was excellent. It also sounded like he spent money on performance mods too. (I don't consider him a "ricer") Now there are Geo Metro's with stock 3-cylinder engines mounting these huge wings. Looks like if the car goes over 30mph the front will come off the ground!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">   <P>Well that's my opinion.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Indiana_resto_guy||11-08-2001||04:03 PM||||I'll just take it back to the original:<P>BUY AMERICAN! KEEP OUR CASH IN HOUSE!<P>That's about as simple as I can make it.||||reg||1
Z||000013||GTFiero1||11-08-2001||04:19 PM||||yeah,the most annoying thing is the coffee can exhaust, i mean, what is the point? and rear spoilers on 4banger hatchbacks. addittude. i dont like the fact that most rice owners think american is crap and they can beat any american car. i mean, they have to twin turbo and nitrous everything before they could come even close to beat a camaro or sumthin. they take there moms accord that they use to get driven in elemntary school in, put a bottle of nitrous on it and act like they have 500hp instead of 180.<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000014||FLASHY||11-08-2001||05:00 PM||||OK. If you don't like how someone puts stickers on their car (import or domestic) that says one thing but doesn't truly represent what's under the hood then you don't like "ricers". That's fine, you don't like how they are <B>pretenders</B>.<P>BUT, if you don't like big wings, ground effects, big exhaust, windshield banners (solid ones), tinted windows, neon lights, single wiper blades sticking half-way up the windshield, and lowered...or some of the above...you just don't like that particular fashion. They are NOT <B>pretenders</B>, they are people who like how those cars look. Simple as that. Why does anyone feel they can place themselves higher because they think their own taste is better? That to me seems like an attitude problem. So make sure you have the right attitude if you're going to shoot down someone else's attitude.<P>Now, I totally agree that the ones with stickers everywhere trying to advertise they have something they really don't is annoying especially when they think they have a faster car because of them. We all seem to agree on that. But I have an appreciation for those individuals who spend $30K on the looks of their cars even if there is no performance upgrades whatsoever. Why? because it's an art. If many of you feel it's worth spending tons of money on performance and not on the looks then that's your "art" preference. I just don't like when someone thinks their art preferences are better than someone else's. That's just ignorant.<P>I just think we should limit our "ricer" calling to those who are PRETENDERS.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||11-08-2001||05:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>But i can offord the stickers quicker then i can the engine.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>as long as you don't put stickers on for something you don't have.. that's fine. but if you have, for example, a GT badge on a 4cyl... that's "domestic rice"... in order to actually need a 4" exhaust, you'd have to be running a 455 or bigger! most cars don't have any real problem with exhaust restrictions due to the size of the pipe, it's usually the muffler, cat, etc.<P>and btw, all the "weird ****" you mentioned, would that be turbos and intercoolers and nos tanks by any chance?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000016||The Fieromaster||11-08-2001||05:36 PM||||I have rice now!  Im infiltrating there clubs and talking good about Fiero... its surprising how you can get them to listen if you own a car that they love!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> Infiltration GOOD! But my car does have an exhaust now (yes potato shooter) and it does have intake.. but soon it will have a turbo (almost all the stuff purchased) all my stickers (just like on my Fiero) are under my hood!!! (decklid on the Fiero)<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Brandon86SE||11-08-2001||05:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>If you don't like how someone puts stickers on their car (import or domestic) that says one thing but doesn't truly represent what's under the hood then you don't like "ricers". That's fine, you don't like how they are pretenders.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Alright, "Turbo".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (Inside Joke)<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000018||Flamberge||11-09-2001||01:57 AM||||One reason most of us (or maybe I should only speak for myself) hate ricers is for the same reason lions hate hyenas. It is a food chain thing. They (the ones with Civics that look like catfish) are lower down than us, for the most part, and are a dime a dozen to boot. Someone up the thread said it best: why do you need a wing that big??<P> It all started with the Supra. (Well, actually the Plymouth Superbird, the least non-rice car ever.) The Supra was also a VERY non-rice car. The top of the line Supra was faster than a WS6 Firebird of the same year. (And twice as much, too.) But it had that "shark" look to it. It caught on, and now everyone has either a Supra-esque wing or worse - the "I race my cars in GTP...no really I do" wing that is wider than the Civic it is attached to. <P>We all have different opinions, but ultimately I think that people can do whatever they want to their vehicles (base model Fieros had pathetic power)as long as they remember that there is always something faster. A good healthy dose of "American Graffiti" (the movie, not the vandalism) might cure them. <P>If they want a humerous wing, flatulent exhaust and pink brakelights, (from the cheap white brakelight covers that are all the rage right now) then more power to them. I will take my wing stock, my exhaust quad trumps and my breaklights a healthy red.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>[Dennis Miller]<BR>Of course that's just my opinion, I could be wrong.<BR>[/Dennis Miller]<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000019||FLASHY||11-09-2001||02:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B> Alright, "Turbo".    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (Inside Joke)<P>Brandon</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think the guy you are talking about USED to have a turbo but it broke down so he ended up going back to a stock 2.8. It just took him a while to remove the "turbo" logo, that's all. That sounds convincing doesn't it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||thomas_l||11-09-2001||10:06 AM||||Rice goes beyond just being fake. When I use rice to describe a car it has the most cheap, uncreative, bogus things done to it. The one "mod" that stands out in my mind would be spray-bombing the plastic interior parts some color you will never see in nature. And a fire extinguisher hanging off the A-pillar next to the mud-dauber nest jet-fighter simulating  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> gauge pod array really scares me at a stop light too. Just what gauges are added there? Altimeter? Time & temp? Compass? Seat belt tension? Heart monitor?<P>People that have truly bad-ass cars don't have to go outta the way to advertise.||||reg||10
Z||000021||blazin'||11-09-2001||11:30 AM||||Where I live, there are a few Integra's, I'll admit, they're nice looking, but all their investing went into looks, stickers, and exhaust.<P>There is a big group of cars that "hang out" in a parking lot, and they consist of 3 integra's, a VW golf, a million civics, a few Camaros, a bunch of 'stangs and a nice Trans Am. I dislike most of the people, but I like their cars. <P>I wanted to talk to them about their cars, but I was laughed away when I pulled in with my Fiero!! And my Fiero is not a bad looking car!<P>The only guy I can talk to is the guy with the T/A, he has a 396 in it and it does something like mid 12's in the 1/4 mile.<P>Back to the subject, I believe that the people who drive the ricers are the ones to dislike. Just because you spent 5 grand on body kits and stereo doesn't mean you can act like you're the king of the town!<P><p>[This message has been edited by blazin' (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||1
